ADDITIONAL CONTRIBUTOR PROTECTIONS AND RIGHTS
(Inspired by Brazilian Labor Law - CLT principles)

1. CONTRIBUTOR ATTRIBUTION
   - All contributors retain authorship rights to their contributions
   - Contributors will be properly credited in the CONTRIBUTORS.md file
   - Commit history preserves individual contribution records

2. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS
   - Contributors retain copyright over their original contributions
   - By contributing, you grant a perpetual license as defined above
   - You may reuse your own contributions in other projects

3. PROTECTION AND RESPONSIBILITY
   - The project maintainer assumes responsibility for the project direction
   - Contributors are not liable for issues arising from project use
   - Clear contribution guidelines protect contributor interests

4. FAIR COLLABORATION
   - All contributors have equal opportunity to participate
   - Contributions are evaluated based on technical merit
   - Transparent decision-making process for project changes

5. WITHDRAWAL RIGHTS
   - Contributors may stop contributing at any time
   - Past contributions remain under the license granted
   - No ongoing obligations after contribution

6. RECOGNITION AND RESPECT
   - Professional conduct required from all participants
   - Harassment or discrimination will not be tolerated
   - See CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md for detailed community standards

For questions about licensing or contributor rights, please open an issue
or contact the project maintainer.
